+# Variant of e87109e9
+# Dimension: D13 — 图例与障碍物的对应关系 (symbol_instructions)
+# Change: 图例中每个颜色条目与主区域中同色障碍物一一对应——图例颜色即障碍物颜色，4个条目对应最多4种障碍物颜色... → 图例颜色与障碍物颜色不同（间接映射）
+#
+# Design analysis
+# a) Concrete form and behavior trace:
+#    - Keep the original 6x24 legend scaffold and the original beam physics.
+#    - Each 4x4 legend cell now contains two colored elements on black:
+#      a full-height edge bar and a central 2x2 swatch.
+#    - The swatch color names the obstacle color in the main grid.
+#    - The bar color is a different "symbol" color; only its left/right position
+#      encodes L/R turn direction.
+#    - Example: a cell with red center swatch and blue right bar means
+#      "red obstacles turn right". In the original task the blue bar itself would
+#      have named the obstacle; here that would be wrong.
+# b) Complexity calibration:
+#    - The indirect mapping is visible in every legend cell, not a one-off clue.
+#    - There are still only 4 legend entries and at most 4 obstacle colors, so the
+#      mapping load stays small enough for ARC.
+#    - Symbol colors are a derangement of the swatch colors, so every cell is
+#      visibly indirect and no cell collapses back to the old same-color regime.
+# c) Old assumptions that must change:
+#    - The original _parse_legend assumed exactly one non-black color per cell.
+#      That is no longer valid because each cell now legitimately has two colors.
+#    - The original solver keyed turns by bar color; that would mis-address
+#      obstacles in the variant.
+#    - The generator originally chose obstacle colors directly from legend-bar
+#      colors; now it must choose obstacle colors from swatches and a separate
+#      per-cell bar color pairing.
+# d) Placement legality:
+#    - The main-grid obstacle placement logic is unchanged, so all non-overlap,
+#      edge-touching, and beam-lane guarantees are preserved.
+#    - The legend layout is fixed-width, so the swatch is always in the 2x2 center
+#      and the bar always occupies exactly the leftmost or rightmost interior column.
+# e) Visual observability:
+#    - A human sees repeated paired glyphs: "center sample color + side bar".
+#      This gives a stable local cue for decoding the mapping from few examples.
+#    - The rule never depends on numeric color ids or hidden ordering.
+# f) Visual cleanliness:
+#    - Each legend cell uses only black, one 2x2 swatch, and one edge bar.
+#      Nothing overlaps, and the two roles are spatially separated.
+# g) Color-change inferability:
+#    - Only 4 swatch colors are involved, and each pairing is explicit inside one
+#      cell. The generator rejects degenerate samples where using the old direct
+#      color assumption would accidentally produce the same beam output.
+
